# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-15; board 1.66); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: three windows docked and one floating on the big display at a desk, one of them filling it; a fifth on the laptop. The cable comes
# out. macOS brings the four windows over to the laptop by itself, and their apps say so. Arbor hears of displays only once they have
# settled, a second and a half later. The windows have jumped, so the person presses the key that shows everything, at once. As in every
# other wait of Arbor's the key is taken, nothing moves, and a line says why; pressed again a moment later it does what it says.
# Before: Arbor answered by the displays it still believed in. Float All sent all four back to the display that was gone.
# Spec: docs/features/F08-displays-and-spaces.md. Window ids start at 101.
quiet
plug desk right 1920x1080
open Code 480x348
open Safari 480x348
open Terminal 480x348
open Chat 480x348
open Notes 480x348
move 101 1600 100 480 348
move 102 1700 150 480 348
move 103 1800 200 480 348
move 104 1900 250 480 348
cursor 2000 500
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 beside 102 bottom
zoom 101
wait 5
loud
expect count docked 3
expect hidden 102
# The cable comes out.
quietly unplug desk
move 101 170 220 480 348
move 102 220 180 480 348
move 103 270 140 480 348
move 104 320 100 480 348
cursor 400 300
wait 0.4
key ctrl+opt+space
expect fail
expect said The displays are still changing
expect at 101 170 220
expect at 102 220 180
expect at 103 270 140
expect at 104 320 100
expect at 105 300 200
# The way out is refused like the rest: nothing is sent to where there is no display.
float-all
expect fail
expect at 101 170 220
expect at 104 320 100
# Now Arbor is told.
wait 1.3
report-displays
wait 1
key ctrl+opt+space
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
expect visible 104
expect size 101 480x348
expect size 102 480x348
expect size 103 480x348
expect at 105 300 200
# Back at the desk, the arrangement is too, with Code filling the display as it did.
plug desk right 1920x1080
wait 3
expect count docked 3
expect visible 101
expect hidden 102
expect hidden 103
